 `message.body.text` omits the receiving bot's mention; `message.body.html` keeps the full rich text. Resolve `message.link` and `room.reply_to` relative to your Campfire origin. `room.reply_to` contains your bot's posting credential: keep it out of logs and don't share it.
 
+## Joining rooms
+
+When a bot with a webhook gains access to an open or closed room, Campfire sends a `joined` callback. Direct conversations never send this event. Campfire attempts delivery once per bot and room; saving memberships again or removing and re-adding a bot that was already notified doesn't send another event. Adding a webhook does not send events for existing memberships.
+
+```json
+{
+  "event": "joined",
+  "room": { "id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/42-Xy3abc9defGh/messages" }
+}
+```
+
+## Replying to callbacks
+
+Both `mention` and `joined` callbacks support immediate or later replies:
+
 - To reply immediately, respond with `200 OK` and a UTF-8 body with `Content-Type: text/plain` or `text/html`. Campfire posts the response as the bot, sanitizing HTML replies.
 - To reply later, return `204 No Content` and send a plain-text `POST` to `room.reply_to` when ready. You can also return `204` without replying.
 
